{"seconds": 47.3, "exit": 0, "final": "Perfect! So Rd5+ wins material in all lines. The main forcing line is:\n1. Rd5+ Kg4 (or Kg6, Kf4)\n2. Rxh4+ (check wins the rook)\n\nThis is a **fork** motif - the rook on d5 gives check, forcing the king to move, then the rook captures the undefended Black rook on h4 with check.\n\n**Best move:** Rd5+\n\n**Main line:** Rd5+ Kg4 Rxh4+\n\n**Motif:** fork (the check forces the king away, allowing capture of the undefended rook)\n\n**Explanation:**\nAfter Black's last move Kg5, White's h8 rook is attacked and seemingly trapped. However, Rd5+ is a discovered-style fork: it gives check to the king on g5, forcing it to move (likely to g4), and then Rxh4+ wins Black's undefended rook with check. After Kg4 Rxh4+, White has won a full rook (+5 material). \n\n**Coaching note:**\nWhen your rook is attacked, look for forcing moves (checks, captures) that create bigger threats. Here, a check that forces the opponent's king away lets your other piece capture the attacker. Always scan for moves that hit multiple targets at once\u2014especially checks combined with attacking loose pieces.\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Rd5+\", \"line\": [\"Rd5+\", \"Kg4\", \"Rxh4+\", \"Kxh4\"], \"motifs\": [\"fork\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "7R/ppp2r2/5p2/6k1/7r/P7/1P6/1K1R4 w - - 2 32"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "7R/ppp2r2/5p2/6k1/7r/P7/1P6/1K1R4 w - - 2 32"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "7R/ppp2r2/5p2/6k1/7r/P7/1P6/1K1R4 w - - 2 32"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "7R/ppp2r2/5p2/6k1/7r/P7/1P6/1K1R4 w - - 2 32", "move": "Rh5+"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "7R/ppp2r2/5p2/6k1/7r/P7/1P6/1K1R4 w - - 2 32", "move": "Rd5+"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "7R/ppp2r2/5p2/6k1/7r/P7/1P6/1K1R4 w - - 2 32", "move": "Rf8"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args